WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.400
OneQuestion: find the missing answer that changes the whole roster.
All volunteer data in this recording is fictional.

00:03.500 --> 00:08.000
These are previously generated real Clocked results from 9 Nov.
No new Extract or Decide request is shown.

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
Inspect exact source phrases and review status.
One availability proposal was accepted; six still await review.

00:17.000 --> 00:23.000
The separate keyless example starts with three of four roles filled.
Its starting interpretations are hand-authored fixtures.

00:24.000 --> 00:33.000
Preview confirming Cy's venue access: four roles become fillable,
with three existing volunteers reassigned. Saved facts do not change.

00:33.000 --> 00:41.000
Return to the actual plan. Dee's sound qualification alone
does not add coverage. Both outcomes are calculated, not predicted.

00:42.000 --> 00:49.000
Record a clearly fictional actual reply, its context and a reviewer.
Saving a reply changes evidence; a preview never does.

00:49.000 --> 00:59.000
The actual saved draft now fills all four roles.
Reload retains the confirmation and the reassigned roster.

00:59.000 --> 01:05.000
The shareable roster contains roles and names.
Original messages and private fact history are omitted.

01:05.000 --> 01:12.000
The recording now makes a real Clocked Fill request on 9 Nov.
Watching it later makes no provider call.

01:12.000 --> 01:24.000
The organizer supplies one dated interval and explicit roles.
Fill proposes editable fields; it does not approve the plan.

01:24.000 --> 01:28.000
Fill returns three proposed roles and a sound-operation requirement.
The coordinator must map each qualification to the appropriate role.

01:28.000 --> 01:32.933
Try the working keyless example, inspect the recorded review,
or run locally with your own Clocked key.
